+# Tayoca Arena Redesign — Items Requiring Owner Confirmation
+
+These items could not be fully verified from repository evidence or public sources. The redesign either excluded them, kept them with disclosure, or made conservative choices — each needs an owner decision before or after reconciliation.
+
+## Claims & disclosure
+
+1. **Withdrawn $216K AWS narrative** — `results.html` previously linked `blog/how-we-saved-216k-on-aws-in-90-days.html` as evidence while the homepage states the narrative is withdrawn from proof use pending re-verification. Redesign removed it from Results. Owner decision: (a) re-verify and restore as a documented case study, or (b) mark both $216K articles as "withdrawn narrative" notices on the articles themselves.
+2. **About-page metric tiles** ("Deploy to prod ≤15 min", "MTTR ≤5 min", "Cloud bill ≤80% baseline") — removed; no traceable evidence found in repo. Restore only with an evidence ledger entry.
+3. **Credential badges** (PMP, CSM, Terraform Associate, AWS Solutions Architect) — retained only on About (removed from footers). Confirm each is current/verifiable and keep an attestation record.
+4. **SiteSupply** — presented on `/work.html` as a venture/build with the blog article as canonical source ("helping bring a B2B procurement marketplace to market… Canada and the United States"). Confirm: disclosure status (client build vs. Tayoca venture), naming rights, and whether a dedicated page is desired.
+5. **Sivanta production status** — `data/sivanta-offers.md` mentions a sandboxed production deployment and a POG Technologies deployment as a portfolio/case-study candidate. The public `sivanta.html` does not name any tenant (correct). Confirm what may be published publicly about deployments before any case study is added.
+6. **AI Made Simple** — landers exist (`landing_ai-made-simple.html`, `landing_ai-made-simple-page.html`) but the product is "staged" per `EPIC_checklist.md` and is not in the stage-10 catalogue. Kept out of products/portfolio. Confirm status (publish, keep staged, or archive landers).
+7. **Legacy landers** — `/l/*` (Tailwind CDN) and superseded product landers remain live behind redirects. Recommend: archive `l/*` to noindex or remove once 301s are confirmed; keep redirects indefinitely.
+
+## Control-plane
+
+8. **Gateway path allowlist** — the Unified Gateway v6.1's exact `public/**` read/write allowlist lives in the runtime workflow, not the repo. Confirm the allowlist so `company-ecosystem.json` and `work.html` can be added to CMS-managed entities deliberately.
+9. **Workflow registry freshness** — `workflow-registry.yaml` last reconciled 2026-08-11; confirm still current (5 active workflows) before the rationalisation plan is executed.
+10. **Products feed** — confirm whether `products-feed.csv` is generated by a workflow (format contract) or hand-maintained, so the new registry can reference it correctly.
+
+## Operating plan
+
+11. This redesign is a public-surface + content-model change. Per `docs/production-growth-operating-plan.yaml`, post-certification work follows the locked plan; this branch is an external review workspace. Confirm the reconciliation path into canonical Forgejo and the intended cycle/wave for deployment.
